{#- WEBSITE › RESOURCES — one of the site's two collections, on a page of its own
   (Chase, 2026-09-27: the Library page "is just a tab navigation", so
   Resources and Events are their own entries in the Website list). One file
   per item under src/content/resources/; admin-library.js draws the list and
   asks the server for this collection only. -#}

<div class="ms-bar">
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" data-lib-add="resources"
          data-i18n="lib.addResource">+ Add resource</button>
</div>
<div class="adm-people" data-lib-list="resources">
  <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading&hellip;</p>
</div>

{#- The languages this build publishes, handed to the script rather than
   fetched: it is the same list Eleventy paginated the public pages over, so
   the editor cannot offer a language the site does not render. -#}
<script id="libLangs" type="application/json">{{ activeLangs | dump | safe }}</script>
